  <prompt>SKILL Step 0.5b substitution block currently substitutes only `{env}` and `{openAiRegion}` in `check_recipe.cli`. But the manifest contains 19 additional placeholder tokens that run literally as shell strings, causing silent false-fails or opaque `az` errors:

`{containerTypeId}`, `{l2UamiPrincipalId}`, `{l2UamiSpId}`, `{l2UamiClientId}`, `{subId}`, `{sub}`, `{artifactsStorageId}`, `{acrId}`, `{bffAppServiceId}`, `{kvResourceId}`, `{sbNamespace}`, `{sbName}`, `{adminDvUrl}`, `{dvUrl}`, `{bffAppId}`, `{graphAppId}`, `{customerId}`, `{region}`, `{pinnedVer}`

Plus PRQ-E-07 has an unescaped `$filter` inside its OData URL that bash `-c` wrapper expands to empty string, collapsing the query.

Plus PRQ-E-13 is scoped `once_per_env` but references `{customerId}` — only known post-Step-1 intake. Step 0.5b runs BEFORE Step 1. Placement mismatch. **PRQ-05 resolution (2026-08-27)**: PRQ-E-13 was DELETED from prereqs.yaml (see commit d5ba336bf); placeholder-record verification lives in SKILL.md Step 1f exclusively. This task 207 therefore no longer needs to fix PRQ-E-13.

**PRQ-11 amendment (2026-08-27) — four `$var` bash-expansion sites explicitly enumerated:**

The Step 0.5b invocation `& bash -c $recipe` runs each recipe in a fresh bash subshell with NO pre-defined variables. Any `$name` in the recipe body is expanded by bash to the empty string, silently corrupting the CLI call. The 4 known sites:

1. **PRQ-T-01 line 58 (pre-fix)** — `Authorization=Bearer $graphAppOnlyToken` — `$graphAppOnlyToken` never defined; produced `Authorization=Bearer ` (empty Bearer) → silent 401. **Resolution**: rewrite recipe to acquire token in-line via `token=$(az account get-access-token --resource https://graph.microsoft.com --query accessToken -o tsv); [ -z "$token" ] && exit 1`. See PRQ-01 (commit 75537850a).

2. **PRQ-T-02 line 73 (pre-fix)** — same `$graphAppOnlyToken` trap. Same resolution. See PRQ-01.

3. **PRQ-C-05 line 462 (pre-fix)** — `Authorization=Bearer $customerTenantToken` — `$customerTenantToken` never defined AND is infeasible operator-side (operator does NOT hold customer-tenant credentials). **Resolution**: PRQ-C-05 marked server-side-only (H0.5 handler in L2 control-plane verifies via multitenant app-only token flow); operator-side check reduced to `echo … ; exit 0` skip. See PRQ-02 (commit 75537850a).

4. **PRQ-E-07 line 288** — `?$filter=principalId eq {l2UamiSpId}` — the `$filter` OData query string parameter is unescaped so bash `-c` expands it to empty, collapsing the query to `?=principalId eq ...` (garbage). **Resolution**: escape as `\$filter=principalId%20eq%20...` (URL-encoded spaces) OR wrap the URI arg in single quotes so bash does not expand.

Same class also proactively applied to PRQ-E-08 in PRQ-07 rewrite (which uses `\$filter` and `\$select`).

Per-placeholder resolution strategy (from audit note § Class C):
- **Skill-side substitution extension**: `{env}`, `{openAiRegion}`, `{region}` (rename to `{openAiRegion}`), `{containerTypeId}` (add to skill from env config; distinct per env)
- **Runtime derivation from az context**: `{subId}` / `{sub}` → `$(az account show --query id -o tsv)`; `{l2UamiPrincipalId}` → `$(az identity show --name <l2-uami> --query principalId)`; `{l2UamiClientId}` → `--query clientId`; `{artifactsStorageId}`/`{acrId}`/`{bffAppServiceId}`/`{kvResourceId}`/`{sbNamespace}` → per-service `az … show --query id`
- **Hardcoded Spaarke constant**: `{graphAppId}` → `00000003-0000-0000-c000-000000000000` (invariant Microsoft Graph app id)
- **Scope-placement change**: PRQ-E-13 → move from `once_per_env` to `once_per_customer` (or introduce a new `once_per_customer_pre_intake` phase); requires SKILL Step 1 to iterate customer-scoped prereqs AFTER intake but BEFORE preflight

Bash-expansion fix for PRQ-E-07: escape as `\$filter` OR single-quote the URL so bash `-c` doesn't expand.</prompt>

  <role>Main-session operator (skill-directives hot-path + prereqs manifest hot-path).</role>

  <goal>Every placeholder token in `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml check_recipe.cli` is either substituted by SKILL Step 0.5b at runtime, derived at runtime from az context inside the recipe itself, hardcoded as a Spaarke constant, or explicitly documented as a scope-placement follow-on. PRQ-E-07 shell-expansion bug fixed. PRQ-E-13 either re-scoped or the skill extended to run customer-scoped prereqs post-intake.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 199 SESSION 14 established the parseable manifest baseline + `validate.ps1` forcing function. Task 206 sweeps recipe-contract violations (exit 1 guards). This task 207 sweeps placeholder-substitution defects — the other independent correctness class the audit surfaced.

      Both 206 and 207 are pre-requisites for prereqs.yaml Step 0.5 iteration to actually deliver value at operator invocation. Without both, Step 0.5 either false-passes (206 gap) or false-fails (207 gap) on every recipe. Combined, the manifest becomes the forcing function it was designed to be.
    </background>
