  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="skill-Step-0.5b">Any new substitution token added to Step 0.5b must have a clear derivation source (intake field, `az` context command, or Spaarke constant). Do NOT add tokens whose value is undecidable at Step 0.5 time (that would just move the false-fail into the substitution block).</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope-taxonomy">If PRQ-E-13 needs to run post-intake, the fix is either (a) re-scope to `once_per_customer` (which currently defers to L2 H0 server-side per skill design) OR (b) introduce a new post-intake pre-preflight phase in the skill. Option (b) is a substantive skill change and warrants its own escalation via §6.5.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-3">Sub-Agent Write Boundary — SKILL.md edits main-session-only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>No `{placeholder}` token remains in `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml check_recipe.cli` that SKILL Step 0.5b substitution block does NOT resolve OR the recipe itself does not derive at runtime.</criterion>
    <criterion>PRQ-E-07 uses `\$filter` or single-quoted URL so bash `-c` does not expand the `$filter` variable.</criterion>
    <criterion>PRQ-E-13 either has scope corrected to `once_per_customer` (deferring to L2 H0 server-side) OR skill Step 0.5 flow is extended with post-intake iteration phase. **PRQ-05 resolution (2026-08-27)**: PRQ-E-13 was DELETED from prereqs.yaml; placeholder-record verification lives in SKILL.md Step 1f only. This criterion is SATISFIED by deletion.</criterion>
    <criterion>`validate.ps1` PASSES.</criterion>
    <criterion>Smoke test: run a customer-scoped intake through Step 0.5 iteration; all applicable prereqs either resolve substitutions or explicitly defer to post-intake per skill design.</criterion>
    <criterion source="PRQ-11 amendment 2026-08-27">**No `$var` reference in `check_recipe.cli` is undefined at recipe-invocation time.** Every `$name` in a recipe MUST be either (a) defined in-recipe via `var=$(...)` before use, (b) explicitly documented in the recipe as intake-supplied via SKILL Step 0.5b substitution (in which case the token is `{name}` not `$name`), OR (c) a well-known bash special variable ($?, $$, $*, etc. — none currently used). The four historical trap sites (PRQ-T-01 `$graphAppOnlyToken`, PRQ-T-02 `$graphAppOnlyToken`, PRQ-C-05 `$customerTenantToken`, PRQ-E-07 `$filter` OData param) enumerated in the prompt block MUST all be resolved. Verification: a `grep -nE '\$[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*' scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml` produces ONLY references that are defined in-recipe or are documented substitution-block outputs.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
